  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1051 PM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nBy the weekend, the anchored ridge will be pushed to our west as \nthe wondering upper level low moves westward across FL and into \nthe northern Gulf. Models are even more split today on what the \nstrength and longevity of this low will be. It seems to stall for \na little bit over the NE Gulf on Saturday before either sliding \nwestward, or weakening and fading out completely. Regardless, \ndangerous heat will persist into the weekend. Look for highs to be\nin the lower 90s in NE AL/portions of Southern Middle TN, and the\nmid to upper 90s elsewhere. Heat index values at this time look \nto remain below heat advisory criteria sitting around 100 degrees,\nhowever we will remain in a level 2-3 HeatRisk across the TN \nValley. So ensure to be heat safe/smart. Slow down, hydrate and \nnever leave people or pets in vehicles.\n\nAn upper level trough will move across the Rockies and Northern \nPlains this weekend and into the Upper Midwest early next week, \nbut there is also uncertainty on this feature. A sfc low will move\ninto the OH Valley on Monday and try to pull a cold front towards\nthe TN Valley. Will see low to medium rain chances return \n(20-45%) on Monday, but with the front most likely stalling on \nTuesday, we won't see a frontal passage, but have rain chances \ncontinue. This will at least help the temps lower a tad with some \nseeing highs in the upper 80s Tuesday afternoon.",
